[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629030581","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102287#issuecomment-2629030581","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102287","id":2629030581,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cs9K1","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-01T17:08:20Z","updated_at":"2025-02-01T17:09:02Z","body":"Can you describe the exact flicker behavior (or record a video of it with a camera)? Does the screen turn fully black, or does it brightness change slightly? If it's only the brightness changing slightly, then this is [VRR flicker](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/troubleshooting.html#the-editor-stutters-and-flickers-on-my-variable-refresh-rate-monitor-g-sync-freesync) which is prevalent on displays that use variable refresh rate. It's a hardware phenomenon: nothing can be done to fix it, but you can disable VRR in the system settings.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629030581/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629073347","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102287#issuecomment-2629073347","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102287","id":2629073347,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ctHnD","user":{"login":"bloemer","id":4493216,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0OTMyMTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4493216?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bloemer","html_url":"https://github.com/bloemer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bloemer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bloemer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bloemer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bloemer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bloemer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bloemer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bloemer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bloemer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bloemer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-01T19:05:43Z","updated_at":"2025-02-01T20:10:41Z","body":"Thank you for your reply. \nThe laptop screen does not have a variable refresh rate. \nI can only switch between 60 and 120 Hz.\nWith 60 Hz, the flickering is not as frequent. The flickering is not that it just gets a little darker, but it gets completely bright/whiteish, or dark/blackish.\n\nThe suggested setting - to change the **Low Processor Mode Sleep** din't removed the flickering, but helped a lot to reduce it.\n\nThank you","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/